{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Only against HaShem do not rebel.</b> If you desire that the land be yours at this degree of good, do not rebel against HaShem — as it says: וְהָיָה אִם שָׁמֹעַ תִּשְׁמְעוּ… וְנָתַתִּי מְטַר אַרְצְכֶם… וְאָסַפְתָּ (Deuteronomy 11:13–14)." "<b>And you — do not fear.</b> If you do not rebel, the El will bring them [the Canaanites] [to defeat]." "<b>For they are our bread.</b> We have seen that they have no intention of rising against us at all, just as bread does not rise against those who eat it — as Rahab testified, saying: וְלֹא קָמָה עוֹד רוּחַ בְּאִישׁ מִפְּנֵיכֶם (Joshua 2:11)." "<b>Their shadow has departed from upon them.</b> We saw that they agreed to abandon every shield and buckler, in order to hasten to flee from us — as in the matter of הַדֶּרֶךְ מְלֵאָה בְגָדִים וְכֵלִים אֲשֶׁר הִשְׁלִיכוּ אֲרָם בְּחָפְזָם (II Kings 7:15)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:50.557968923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}